{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789810334,"nonce":"dWkVJyY5AzBwjjsZQ8he9hnSUOA=","title":"MIR inliner: a later site's failure edge passed the first site's generic result","message":"With two inlined sites in one versioned loop, the second site's guard-failure edge into the generic copy handed over the *first* site's generic call result (a value defined only in the first site's slow block) instead of the fast continuation's parameter. `inline_site` overwrote `slow_to_fast[slow_dst]` with the slow result, which is right for that site's own edge only. Cranelift's verifier reports it as \"uses value arg from non-dominating block\"; in release builds it reached regalloc as EntryLivein and the compile failed, and the same stray value made every loop header's OSR live-in set include a value the interpreter cannot supply, so OSR was declined at every iteration (mandelbrot at 50 s).\n\nOnly surfaced once accessors were inlined (WLIFT_INLINE_ACCESSORS=1); arithmetic-only bodies rarely put two sites in one loop.\n\nFix: entries carry `(copy value, generic result)` and only that edge substitutes it. Result guards from `speculate_call_results` now also land on the continuation parameter an inlined call's result becomes.","files":null}]}